                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Can I tint my full windshield in California?</summary>
                        <p>California rules are narrow around windshield film. The safe answer is to verify the exact
                            placement and material requirements before choosing any windshield film.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Are front windows treated the same as rear windows?</summary>
                        <p>No. Front side windows are treated more strictly. Side windows behind the driver have
                            different exceptions under the code.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Should I choose shade before checking legality?</summary>
                        <p>No. Choose the look and comfort goal first, then confirm which windows can legally receive
                            that film choice.</p>
